  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Located on avenue de Verdun in Fréjus, near the amphitheatre and the train station, Clinique Vétérinaire des Arènes offers a full technical setup (consultation rooms, surgery suite, analysis lab, medical imaging and hospitalisation) alongside general medicine.</p>
      <p>Its particularity: gentle-medicine consultations and treatments, with herbal medicine, homeopathy, osteopathy and acupuncture, which the team presents as natural alternatives to drug treatments. The website specifies that the clinic treats dogs, cats and rabbits, for preventive visits as well as emergency consultations, and that it also advises on diet, training, hygiene or reproduction. Prices are published in the "À propos" section of the website.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The clinic is open Monday to Friday from 9am to 7pm, and Saturday morning from 8am to 12pm; it is closed on Sunday. Appointments are made by phone on 04 94 53 70 55 or online, via the Mon Rendez-vous Véto platform, whose link the website gives.</p>
      <p>For emergencies, the clinic's website gives 04 89 88 34 34. Outside opening hours, the website's "Urgences" page indicates that this number reaches an emergency service located in Puget-sur-Argens: the clinic therefore does not itself provide night, Sunday and public-holiday cover.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: if your dog tends to get stressed at the vet, it may be worth asking the team about the complementary approaches offered here (osteopathy in particular).</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The clinic is near the amphitheatre and the train station of Fréjus, making it an easy landmark to find when arriving by train or visiting the town.</p>
    </div>

